# Expected failures of the Eclipse Paho interoperability suite on the dev
# image's development port (scripts/mqtt5-conformance.sh --boot --listener dev:
# client id = identity, sessions persist, the device ACL opened to #).
# docs/MQTT5-CONFORMANCE.md section 2.
# suite        test                            phase   reason
client_test5   test_server_topic_alias         always  the broker never sends topic aliases (ADR-273 rule 9: no per-subscriber alias state)
client_test5   test_subscribe_failure          always  the device ACL is opened to # for the suite (its cleanup subscribes to #; ACLs have no deny rules), so test/nosubscribe is granted; a refused filter gets 0x87 Not authorized, not 0x80 (ADR-273 rule 13), covered by smoke mqtt5-suback-0x87
client_test    test_subscribe_failure          always  as above: the ACL allows # for the suite's cleanup
client_test    test_zero_length_clientid       always  on the development port the client id is the identity (as on TLS, where it must equal the certificate's): a 3.1.1 CONNECT without one names nobody and gets 0x02 Identifier rejected, which 3.1.1 3.1.3.1 allows; unchanged from 3.1.1-only builds. A 5.0 client is assigned one (it passes client_test5), and the plaintext listener accepts it (the reference run passes)
